<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept id="t00116">
	<title id="e00824">Armrest</title>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00825">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e00826">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV025021.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e00827"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2"/>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<p>To use the armrest, pull it forward from the seatback.</p>
		<note type="caution" id="e00828">
			<p>The armrest may be damaged if you sit on it or apply excessive load.</p>
		</note>
		<section id="e00829">
			<title>Carrying long/narrow cargo</title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00830">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e00831">
									<figgroup>
										<image href="../../images/OOV025088.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e00832"/>
									</figgroup>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<p>Additional cargo space is provided to accommodate long/narrow cargo (skis, poles, etc.) not able to fit properly in the tailgate when closed.</p>
			<ol id="e00833">
				<li>Pull the armrest down.</li>
				<li>
					<p>Pull the cover down while pushing the release lever down.</p>
				</li>
			</ol>
			<note type="warning" id="e00834">
				<p>Cargo should always be secured to prevent it from being thrown about the vehicle in a collision and causing injury to the vehicle occupants. Do not place objects in the rear seats, since they cannot be properly secured and may hit the front seat occupants in a collision.</p>
			</note>
		</section>
	</conbody>
</concept>